NVD API Interaction
When writing code that interacts with the NVD API, adhere to the following:

Use the NVD CVE API v2.0: Ensure all API calls are directed to the latest version of the NVD API.

Parameterize CPEs: All functions that query the NVD API should accept a list of CPE strings as a parameter.

API Key Management: Retrieve the NVD API key from environment variables. Do not hard-code the API key.

Error Handling: Implement robust error handling for API requests. This should include handling for rate limiting (429 Too Many Requests) and other HTTP error codes.

Pagination: Be mindful of the resultsPerPage and startIndex parameters to handle paginated results from the API.

